{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented in local worktree `.rebar/worktrees/fix-794e` at commit `65e452ee1505a9305447e9b4a64a9e5961638690` (not pushed).\n\nEvidence:\n- Reproduced live mis-scope: `lmn-staging-private-context-denied` in us-east-1 still watched raw `AWS/S3 4xxErrors` for `BucketName=lmn-staging-private-context-896586841071`, `FilterId=all-private-context-requests`, threshold `Sum > 5` over 300s.\n- Bucket policy readback retained `OnlyCuratorAndGeneratorDataAccess` and `OnlyApprovedPrincipalsCanInspectInventory`, with no audited application roles added to either allowlist.\n- Added Terraform-owned filtered metric path: S3 access-log bucket notification on `lmn-staging-private-context-logs-896586841071/access/` invokes `lmn-private-context-denied-metric`, which publishes `lmn/staging:private_context_unexpected_denials`; the alarm keeps name `lmn-staging-private-context-denied` but watches that custom metric at `Sum > 5` over 300s.\n- Regression test failed before the fix with missing `monitoring_lmn_private_context.tf` and missing handler, then passed after the fix.\n- Validation passed: `pytest -p no:randomly tests/infra/test_lmn_private_context_denied.py`, `make lint`, and `make typecheck`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789926395990085943,"uuid":"07042447-9f58-48e8-bc55-30403d8fce20"}